  "id": "COMPOUND:40572 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "Caragasinin B is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Ataxin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Caragasinin B directly targets M059J, which in turn is a target of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, a compound that ultimately targets Ataxin-2. This indicates a potential regulatory relationship where Caragasinin B may influence the activity of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, which then affects Ataxin-2. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ataxin-2 supports the idea that Caragasinin B could play a role in modulating the expression or function of Ataxin-2 through these intermediaries. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Caragasinin B might exert its effects on Ataxin-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
